6 - File Guide
    ----------

    M001_00_Premises.v

      Closed `Bot`/`Imp` syntax, contexts, functional and finite axiom sources,
      logical profiles, regulator theories, and finite proof-script grammar.

    M001_01__Kernel.v

      Structural formula equality and size, context membership, K/S/optional
      EFQ recognition, proof-line validation, the total script checker, and the
      finite-axiom-set checker.

    M001_02__Abstraction.v

      Executable deduction transformation and its checker-level correctness
      theorem. The internal index map connects source lines to generated proof
      blocks.

    M001_03__Falsity.v

      Executable reductio specialization: checked `Bot` under `A :: Gamma`
      becomes checked `A -> Bot` under `Gamma`.

    M001_04__Certificates.v

      Retained proof-certificate subtype, existential checked derivability, and
      the derivability-level deduction lift.

    M001_05__Application.v

      Script shifting, executable MP composition, checked MP closure, and
      one-line assumption and axiom derivations.

    M001_06__Syntactic_Adequacy.v

      Independent inductive derivability and its exact equivalence with
      existential Boolean-checked derivability.

    M001_07__Monotonicity.v

      Context and regulator-theory inclusion, with preservation theorems for
      concrete checked scripts and existential derivability.

    M001_08__Regulation.v

      Frozen `SymbolicRegulator` interface: output type, instruction type,
      Boolean acceptance function, alias `S_λ`, and existential acceptance.

    M001_09__Regulated_Execution.v

      Canonical proof-regulator instance, pure accepted-output release gate, and
      bridges among Boolean acceptance, release, symbolic derivability, and
      checked derivability.

    M001_95_API.v

      Stable package API and the five canonical contracts `SYNTAX`, `ADEQUACY`,
      `DEDUCTION`, `REDUCTIO`, and `STRUCTURE`.

    M001_97_Artifacts.v

      Certifies `M001_CONTRACT`, redirects its assumption report, and extracts
      the five proof-machine roots to `M001_checker.{ml,mli}`.

    M001_98_Sanity.v

      Closed probes for syntax, checking, transformations, adequacy,
      monotonicity, canonical symbolic regulation, and release.

    _appendix/_artifacts/

      Extracted OCaml: `M001_checker.{ml,mli}`. Extraction remains restricted to
      the checker, finite checker, MP composition, deduction, and reductio.

    _appendix/_assumptions/

      Redirected `Print Assumptions` output for `m001_contract_qed`.


7 - Public API
    ----------

    The stable downstream import is:

      `From M001 Require Import M001_95_API.`

    Public surface by use case:

    Syntax and theories:

      Formula, Bot, Imp, formula_negation                                   (00)
      Context, ctx_extend                                                   (00)
      AxiomSet, FiniteAxiomSet                                              (00)
      RegulatorLogicProfile, RegulatorTheory                                (00)
      Justification, ProofLine, Proof                                       (00)

    Executable checking and transformation:

      regulator_theory_check_bool :
        RegulatorTheory -> Context -> Proof -> Formula -> bool              (01)
      finite_axiom_set_check_bool :
        RegulatorLogicProfile -> FiniteAxiomSet ->
        Context -> Proof -> Formula -> bool                                 (01)
      regulator_theory_deduction_transform : Formula -> Proof -> Proof      (02)
      regulator_theory_reductio_transform : Formula -> Proof -> Proof       (03)
      regulator_theory_mp_compose : Formula -> Proof -> Proof -> Proof      (05)

    Derivability and structure:

      regulator_theory_proof_certificate                                    (04)
      regulator_theory_checked_derivable                                    (04)
      regulator_theory_inductive_derivable                                  (06)
      context_included, regulator_theory_included                           (07)

    Symbolic regulation and release:

      SymbolicRegulator, S_λ                                                (08)
      symbolic_regulator_derivable                                          (08)
      regulator_theory_symbolic_regulator :
        RegulatorTheory -> Context -> S_λ                                   (09)
      symbolic_regulator_release : forall S,
        symbolic_regulator_instruction S ->
        symbolic_regulator_output S ->
        option (symbolic_regulator_output S)                                (09)

    Certified contracts:

      SYNTAX, ADEQUACY, DEDUCTION, REDUCTIO, STRUCTURE                      (95)
      M001_CONTRACT                                                         (95)
      m001_contract_qed                                                     (97)

    Principal theorems:

      formula_not_self_negation : forall A,
        A <> formula_negation A

      regulator_theory_syntactic_adequacy_lemma : forall R Gamma A,
        regulator_theory_checked_derivable R Gamma A <->
        regulator_theory_inductive_derivable R Gamma A

      regulator_theory_deduction_checked : forall R Gamma A B p,
        regulator_theory_check_bool R (ctx_extend A Gamma) p B = true ->
        regulator_theory_check_bool R Gamma
          (regulator_theory_deduction_transform A p) (Imp A B) = true

      regulator_theory_reductio_checked : forall R Gamma A p,
        regulator_theory_check_bool R (ctx_extend A Gamma) p Bot = true ->
        regulator_theory_check_bool R Gamma
          (regulator_theory_reductio_transform A p)
          (formula_negation A) = true

      symbolic_regulator_release_acceptance_iff : forall S i b,
        symbolic_regulator_release S i b = Some b <->
        symbolic_regulator_accepts_bool S i b = true

      regulator_theory_symbolic_regulator_release_iff : forall R Gamma A,
        regulator_theory_checked_derivable R Gamma A <->
        exists p,
          symbolic_regulator_release
            (regulator_theory_symbolic_regulator R Gamma) p A = Some A


8 - Notes
    -----

    The five-contract aggregate is unchanged by the release layer. Release is a
    derived executable view of the frozen Boolean acceptance interface, not a
    new logical rule.

    L001 imports only `M001_00_Premises` and therefore does not depend on the
    checker or release layers. L002 imports `M001_95_API`, packages coded
    recognition as a symbolic regulator, and uses the release gate to expose
    accepted recognition claims without changing their proof-theoretic meaning.

    M001 contains no evaluation frame, world model, closure-equivalence adapter,
    causal provenance, listener side effect, or output synthesis. Such
    interpretations belong to downstream developments.
